## 6. RESTRICTIONS & COMPATIBILITY:
restrictions:
  max_io_current: "1200mA"
  total_current_limit: "1200mA"
  warnings[9]:
    - "1756-L81E has NO integrated field I/O and NO built-in power supply — a separate 1756-PA50, 1756-PA75, 1756-PB50, or 1756-PB75 power supply must be installed in the chassis; the chassis (1756-A4 through 1756-A17) must also be ordered separately; without a chassis and power supply the CPU cannot operate"
    - "The embedded 1Gb EtherNet/IP port supports up to 60 EtherNet/IP nodes directly — each 1756-ENxT communication module in the chassis adds its own node pool (256 nodes per 1756-EN2T, up to 1000 I/O nodes per 1756-EN4TR); total node count across all paths is 100 for L81E; exceeding node limits causes I/O connection faults; use L83E or L85E for larger systems"
    - "CIP Motion (Integrated Motion over EtherNet/IP) reduces available EtherNet/IP I/O bandwidth — each motion axis consumes controller resources (memory, scan time, packet rate); the L81E (3MB) is appropriate for small motion applications of 4-16 axes; for 32+ axes use at minimum the L83E (10MB); for 256 axes the L85E (40MB) is required"
    - "The 1756-L81E-NSE (No Stored Energy) variant has NO internal Energy Storage Module — RTC will lose time on every power loss; the NSE variant was designed for applications where the Energy Arbitration standard (IEC 62368-1 or UL 991) prohibits stored energy devices; substituting NSE for standard L81E in time-critical or coordinated-motion applications will cause timestamp faults and motion discontinuity after every power cycle"
    - "Controller redundancy with the 1756-RM2 or 1756-RM3 is supported but has significant restrictions: Integrated Motion over EtherNet/IP is NOT supported in redundancy mode; CIP Safety is NOT supported; DeviceNet and ControlNet local modules are NOT supported; both primary and secondary chassis must have identical I/O module types and firmware revisions; firmware mismatch causes immediate redundancy disqualification"
    - "CIP Security requires firmware V32 and Studio 5000 V32 minimum — enabling CIP Security reduces I/O packet rate from 28,000 pps to 14,000 pps (integrity only) or 7,000 pps (integrity + confidentiality); all devices in the security zone must support CIP Security; devices without CIP Security support must be placed in a separate unprotected zone; mixed secure and unsecured devices in the same EtherNet/IP zone is not supported"
    - "OPC UA server requires firmware V32 and Studio 5000 V32 — the L81E supports a maximum of 300 OPC UA nodes; each OPC UA node corresponds to one controller tag accessible from outside; for more OPC UA nodes use L82E (1000 nodes), L83E (2000), L84E (5000) or L85E (20,000); OPC UA requires a certificate deployed to the controller from Studio 5000 — connections without valid certificates are rejected by default"
    - "The USB port on the 1756-L81E is Type-A (USB 2.0) for temporary programming only — it must NOT be used as a permanent network connection; wire category 3 rating means high-noise environments require shielded cable; do NOT use the USB port in classified hazardous locations (Class I Div 2 ATEX Zone 2) as the USB port is not rated for use in explosive atmospheres; use EtherNet/IP for all permanent communications"
    - "The 1756-L81E requires a NEMA 1 or equivalent windowless metal enclosure to comply with CE EMC (EN 61000-6-4 Industrial Emissions) — operating the controller outside of a metal enclosure invalidates CE certification; the open-style (IP20) rating of the module provides NO protection against dust, liquids, or physical contact; always install in a suitable industrial enclosure with proper ventilation to maintain the 0-60°C operating range"
compatibility:
  sw: "Studio 5000 Logix Designer V21+ (V21-V35+); RSLogix 5000 V16-V20 (legacy read-only); FactoryTalk View SE/ME for HMI; FactoryTalk Historian; FactoryTalk AssetCentre; PLCSIM Advanced not supported for ControlLogix 5580"
  languages: "Relay Ladder Logic (RLL/LD);Function Block Diagram (FBD);Structured Text (ST);Sequential Function Chart (SFC)"
  frameworks: "IEC61131-3;EtherNet-IP-CIP;CIP-Motion;CIP-Security-TLS-DTLS;CIP-Sync;OPC-UA;PCCC;ControlNet-via-1756-CN2;DeviceNet-via-1756-DNB;SERCOS-via-1756-MxK;FactoryTalk;Studio5000;PlantPAx"
  certifications: "cULus;FM-Class-I-Div2;CE;RCM;ATEX-II-3G-Ex-ec-IIC-T4;IECEx;UKCA;KC;CCC;EtherNet-IP-ODVA;CIP-Security-ODVA"

